      "comment": "WILBERT (1) was safely held in tougher company last start after missing the jump at Gosford, but prior to that won easily by 3.5 lengths at Gosford (35.15) beating Turn Up Ace in a Mix on July 14. Has a strong record from box 1, including two wins. Can bounce back. RADIANT ETHICS (2) found the frame for the second consecutive time when narrowly beaten into second last time out (29.71) over 515m at Gosford. Well placed here and can atone this time. ZIPPING HORNET (7) won again in quick time after leading making it three straight, scoring at Richmond over 520m (30.02). Yet to taste defeat from two runs out of this box. One of the leading chances again. SWIFT WIND (8) collected a minor prize last start and must be considered.",
